5. Multi-branch inter-scale divergence (advisory)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Inter-branch position spread at every quantized Add/Concat, reported by
`check-shift-cut --branches`. A DPU must bring two branches to a common output scale
before it can add or concatenate them, so a wide spread is where that alignment costs
the most precision. NOTHING here is a hazard: no divergence has been measured to
change an output on this device, and BiSeNetV2 -- the model this check was asked for
-- reads zero violations under every criterion in the module.

